OrkaTerra Energy (OTE) is a vertically integrated developer, owner and operator of geothermal power projects, with a focus on Latin America and East Africa. It is OTE's objective to unlock geothermal energy's tremendous potential through the application of superior project development expertise, power plant technology, and investment capital. 

OTE has the capability to design, develop, construct and operate large and complex geothermal resources and power projects. The OTE team and its alliance partners have played lead roles in the development of the some of the world’s largest and most significant geothermal projects. OTE is supported by dedicated project teams and a network of strategic alliance partners offering best-in-class technical and engineering support around the world. 

OTE is part of the Kaishan Group of geothermal businesses and operates in association with KS Orka in Asia and Europe and Open Mountain in North America. OTE’s integrated ownership with Kaishan provides seamless access to Kaishan‘s technological capabilities. Kaishan’s steam-based screw expander generator technology and their Organic Rankine Cycle (“ORC“) based screw expander technology are particularly well suited to optimizing the development of geothermal fields worldwide.

OTE is focused on the development of geothermal power projects using the well-head unit (“WHU”) technology developed by Kaishan. Traditionally, medium and high-temperature geothermal power generation Projects utilize large steam turbines, which are primarily manufactured by Japanese companies. In comparison with conventional utility-scale steam turbine technology, Kaishan’s WHU technology demonstrates significant advantages:

	Shorter time to COD: Construction times can be shortened significantly speeding up the time to achieve COD and provide electricity to the grid;
	Greater Operating Flexibility: Kaishan units can utilize geothermal wells with any pressure allowing for the more efficient use of the steam field resource. Even in the absence of steam, electricity can be generated from hot water;
	Higher Operating Efficiency: Kaishan units are more efficient and outperform steam turbines as Kaishan’s plant can generate electricity from both steam and hot water;
	Capital Cost Efficient: By installing units on wellpads, there is no need to construct expensive steam-gathering pipes and related infrastructure, lowering capital investment as well as ongoing steam loss and maintenance costs; and
	Lower Manufacturing Cost: Kaishan’s units are lower cost and provide better value than centralized turbines. 

Visit our website orkaterra.com to learn more about OrkaTerra Energy.

Patagonia Sur, LLC, is a for-profit venture that invests in, protects, and enhances scenically remarkable and ecologically valuable properties in Chilean Patagonia. Our business model merges conservation and capitalism seamlessly and symbiotically.

Patagonia Sur’s office and team are headquartered in Coyhaique, Chile -- the heart of Patagonia.

Our activities include:
Ecologically-appropriate limited development;
A membership-based eco-tourism club;
Eco-brokerage services;
Carbon sequestration and the sale of carbon offsets;
Ecologically-friendly aquaculture, agriculture, and forestry operations.

Patagonia Sur has also established the Patagonia Sur Foundation. The Foundation’s mission is to encourage conservation and to promote social and economic development in harmony with the region’s majestic natural environment.

